s rather than analgesic benefit."},{"id":"D","text":"Alertness and respiratory effort during rest","explanation":"These assess important adverse effects rather than analgesic benefit itself."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Assess the intended analgesic or antipyretic response before and after treatment.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-acamol--7-day--pain_response","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-acamol::pain_response"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ibd2-acamol--standard--pain_response","answerKey":"B"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Paracetamol is given for fever in a patient without pain. Which comparison most directly measures the intended response?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Respiratory rate before and after the dose","explanation":"Respiratory rate may be clinically relevant but is not the direct measure of fever reduction."},{"id":"B","text":"Pain score before and after the dose","explanation":"Pain is an analgesic outcome; it does not measure fever response in this patient."},{"id":"C","text":"Temperature before and after the dose","explanation":"Temperature is the outcome for antipyretic treatment."},{"id":"D","text":"Blood pressure before and after the dose","explanation":"Blood pressure does not directly measure the antipyretic response."}],"point":"Assess temperature response when paracetamol is given for fever.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-acamol--7-day--acetam_fever_response","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-acamol::acetam_fever_response"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ibd2-acamol--standard--acetam_fever_response","answerKey":"C"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which statement correctly compares paracetamol with NSAIDs?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Inflammation control with stronger peripheral COX inhibition","explanation":"Paracetamol acts predominantly as a central analgesic/antipyretic, rather than a stronger peripheral anti-inflammatory drug."},{"id":"B","text":"Pain/fever relief without the typical NSAID pla