ailability":"WARD-OBSERVED in IBD2 at Nasser Medical Complex on 1 Oct 2026. Exact capsule/tablet strength was not recorded; verify the product and order."},"readingSections":[{"field":"drugclass","label":"Drug class","text":"Gabapentinoid anticonvulsant; neuropathic-pain agent.","id":"section-0-2c14eaada8e71b96"},{"field":"mechanism","label":"Mechanism of action","text":"Binds the alpha-2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels, reducing release of excitatory neurotransmitters.","id":"section-1-cda945c25de391d8"},{"field":"use","label":"Main use","text":"Neuropathic pain/nerve-related pain and seizure indications. In an orthopaedic/trauma setting it may be used when pain has a neuropathic component, but confirm the patient's actual indication.","id":"section-2-26ae2133cce22b3a"},{"field":"administration","label":"Form & administration","text":"PO. Dose selection and interval depend strongly on renal function; do not use a memorized standard dose for every patient. Chronic therapy should not be stopped abruptly without a plan.","id":"section-3-1ef1e042b30fb08b"},{"field":"monitor","label":"Nursing considerations","text":"• Watch somnolence, dizziness, ataxia and falls. • Review renal function. • Serious respiratory depression has been reported when gabapentin is combined with CNS depressants, especially opioids. • With tramadol or other opioids, monitor sedation and breathing more closely. • Peripheral edema can occur.","id":"section-4-ec316d039684976b"},{"field":"why","label":"Essential rationale","text":"Gabapentin reduces excitatory neurotransmitter release through the alpha-2-delta subunit of voltage-gated calcium channels; it is useful for neuropathic rather than purely inflammatory pain.","id":"section-5-3f729c3fb9cc0af3"},{"field":"availability","label":"Palestine availability","text":"WARD-OBSERVED in IBD2 at Nasser Medical Complex on 1 Oct 2026. Exact capsule/tablet strength was not recorded; verify the product and order.","id":"section-6-ceafaeb078d6024f"}],"legacyExams":[{"id":"ibd2-gabapentin--standard","itemId":"ibd2-gabapentin","itemType":"medication","title":"GABAPENTIN","stage":"standard","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">=","percent":90,"roundBeforeComparison":false},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":"persisted total deadline: 90 seconds multiplied by question count"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"show keys and all option explanations after submission","retestPolicy":"same standard form after required reading","questions":[{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"What is the principal mechanism of action of GABAPENTIN?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Relaxes arteriolar smooth muscle","explanation":"This is a different pharmacological action. The drug’s action is: This modulates excitatory neurotransmitter release; it is not a direct GABA agonist."},{"id":"B","text":"Binds the alpha-2-delta calcium-channel subunit","explanation":"This modulates excitatory neurotransmitter release; it is not a direct GABA agonist."},{"id":"C","text":"Inhibits bacterial cell-wall synthesis","explanation":"This is a different pharmacological action. The drug’s action is: This modulates excitatory neurotransmitter release; it is not a direct GABA agonist."},{"id":"D","text":"Modulates membrane stability and repolarization","explanation":"This is a different pharmacological action. The drug’s action is: This modulates excitatory neurotransmitter release; it is not a direct GABA agonist."}],"point":"Identify the principal pharmacological action taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-gabapentin--standard--principal-action","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-gabapentin::principal-action"],"answerKey":"B"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which drug class does GABAPEN