id trend supports congestion beyond ankle appearance."},{"id":"C","text":"Unchanged breathing with stable weight and clear lungs","explanation":"This weakens, rather than establishes, a worsening congestion explanation."},{"id":"D","text":"Edema beginning after a medication change with stable breathing","explanation":"The timing supports a possible drug contribution without establishing HF."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Peripheral edema needs clinical interpretation rather than automatic attribution to volume overload.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-gabapentin--7-day--edema","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-gabapentin::edema"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ibd2-gabapentin--advanced--edema","answerKey":"B"}],"questionCount":8}],"scoringExclusions":[]},{"itemId":"ibd2-avilac","title":"AVILAC — lactulose","itemType":"medication","capabilityRequirement":null,"exams":[{"id":"ibd2-avilac--comprehensive","itemId":"ibd2-avilac","itemType":"medication","title":"AVILAC — lactulose","stage":"comprehensive","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"type":"error-count","allowedErrors":1},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":"untimed"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"incorrect, unanswered and unsure/guessed questions only after submission","retestPolicy":"same comprehensive exam and questions at every stage","questions":[{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"What is the principal mechanism of action of AVILAC — lactulose?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Suppresses gastric H/K ATPase","explanation":"This describes Proton-pump inhibitor. A nonabsorbable disaccharide promotes stool passage through colonic osmotic effects."},{"id":"B","text":"Promotes upper-GI motility","explanation":"This describes D2 antagonist/prokinetic. A nonabsorbable disaccharide promotes stool passage through colonic osmotic effects."},{"id":"C","text":"Blocks serotonin-mediated emesis","explanation":"This describes 5-HT3 antagonist. A nonabsorbable disaccharide promotes stool passage through colonic osmotic effects."},{"id":"D","text":"Retains water in the colon","explanation":"A nonabsorbable disaccharide promotes stool passage through colonic osmotic effects."}],"point":"Identify the principal pharmacological action taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-avilac--comprehensive--principal-action","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-avilac::principal-action"],"answerKey":"D"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which drug class does AVILAC — lactulose belong to?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"D2 antagonist/prokinetic","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Osmotic laxative; non-absorbable disaccharide."},{"id":"B","text":"Osmotic laxative","explanation":"Osmotic laxative; non-absorbable disaccharide."},{"id":"C","text":"Proton-pump inhibitor","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Osmotic laxative; non-absorbable disaccharide."},{"id":"D","text":"Peripheral antimuscarinic","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Osmotic laxative; non-absorbable disaccharide."}],"point":"Identify the drug class taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-avilac--comprehensive--drug-class","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-avilac::drug-class"],"answerKey":"B"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which is a clinical use of AVILAC — lactulose?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Prevention of valve-related thromboembolism","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"B","text":"Treatment of constipation","explanation":"This is a clinical use of the medicine: Constipation. In orthopaedic patients, constipation may be promoted by immobility and opioid analgesics. Lactulose is also used in hepatic encephalopathy for a different indication."},{"id":"C","text":"Replacement of glucose durin