onvulsant","explanation":"Anticonvulsant; voltage-gated sodium-channel blocker; neuropathic-pain agent."},{"id":"C","text":"Gabapentinoid","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Anticonvulsant; voltage-gated sodium-channel blocker; neuropathic-pain agent."},{"id":"D","text":"Dissociative anesthetic","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Anticonvulsant; voltage-gated sodium-channel blocker; neuropathic-pain agent."}],"point":"Identify the drug class taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--drug-class","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::drug-class"],"answerKey":"B"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which is a clinical use of TEGRETOL — carbamazepine?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Rapid IV replacement of circulating glucose","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"B","text":"Treatment of a susceptible bacterial infection","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"C","text":"Seizure or selected neuropathic-pain treatment","explanation":"This is a clinical use of the medicine: Seizure disorders and selected neuropathic-pain conditions such as trigeminal neuralgia. In an orthopaedic patient, confirm whether it is being continued for epilepsy or prescribed for a specific neuropathic-pain indication."},{"id":"D","text":"Inhibition of platelet aggregation after coronary stenting","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."}],"point":"Identify the main treatment role taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--treatment-role","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::treatment-role"],"answerKey":"C"},{"stem":"Which new finding during TEGRETOL — carbamazepine therapy most strongly suggests a serious cutaneous drug reaction?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Rash with mucosal involvement","explanation":"This raises concern for severe hypersensitivity, including SJS/TEN."},{"id":"B","text":"Dry intact skin with mild itching","explanation":"This lacks the mucosal involvement that raises particular concern."},{"id":"C","text":"An unchanged rash documented before treatment","explanation":"An unchanged pre-existing rash is less suggestive of a newly developing severe drug reaction."},{"id":"D","text":"Localized redness at an adhesive edge","explanation":"Localized contact irritation is less suggestive of a severe skin-and-mucosal drug reaction."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"A new severe rash can indicate a serious anticonvulsant reaction.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--rash_serious","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::rash_serious"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"Which ordered investigation best checks the cytopenia risk described with TEGRETOL — carbamazepine?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Coagulation profile","explanation":"Clotting times do not replace measurement of cell counts."},{"id":"B","text":"Complete blood count","explanation":"It measures relevant blood-cell lines, including platelets and white cells."},{"id":"C","text":"Renal function profile","explanation":"Renal function is a different monitoring domain."},{"id":"D","text":"Hepatic function profile","explanation":"Liver tests do not directly quantify the blood-cell lines."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Treatment can cause cytopenias; use the ordered CBC/platelet monitoring.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--cbc","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::cbc"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which abnormality is particularly relevant when a patient taking TEGRETOL — carbamazepine develops confusion and weakness?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Hyperphosphatemia","explanation":"Phosphate elevation is not the specific risk identified here."},{"id":"B","text":"Hyponatremia","explanation":"Low sodium can cause neurological symptoms."},{"id":"C","text":"Hypoalbuminemia","explanation":"Albumi