 susceptible treatment.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--low_na","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::low_na"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"A patient taking TEGRETOL — carbamazepine is newly drowsy and ataxic but has stable vital signs. Which activity most directly requires additional assistance?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Using the call bell while seated with support","explanation":"This does not require the impaired balance involved in standing."},{"id":"B","text":"Choosing a meal while seated with support","explanation":"This does not carry the same immediate fall exposure."},{"id":"C","text":"Reporting pain while seated with support","explanation":"The described impairment most directly compromises unsupported mobility."},{"id":"D","text":"Standing and transferring to the bathroom","explanation":"Impaired alertness and coordination increase fall risk."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Sedation, dizziness, and ataxia can increase fall risk.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--sedation_falls","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::sedation_falls"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"Why can adding carbamazepine alter the effectiveness of another medicine cleared by inducible hepatic enzymes?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"It can increase enzyme-mediated metabolism","explanation":"Enzyme induction can lower exposure to affected concomitant medicines."},{"id":"B","text":"It blocks all renal filtration of the other medicine","explanation":"This is not the hepatic enzyme-induction mechanism."},{"id":"C","text":"It directly supplies the other medicine’s active ingredient","explanation":"The drugs are not interchangeable sources of active ingredient."},{"id":"D","text":"It binds all other medicines inside the gut","explanation":"This is not the general interaction mechanism described."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Carbamazepine can alter other medicines through enzyme induction.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--enzyme_induction","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::enzyme_induction"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"A patient takes chronic TEGRETOL — carbamazepine for epilepsy and has omitted several doses because seizures stopped. Which concern is most relevant?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"An expected increase in anticonvulsant exposure","explanation":"Missed doses generally reduce exposure rather than increase it."},{"id":"B","text":"A reduction in the medicine’s enzyme-inducing potential alone","explanation":"That does not address the immediate loss of established seizure treatment."},{"id":"C","text":"An immediate increase in renal drug clearance","explanation":"Dose omission does not itself establish a renal-clearance change."},{"id":"D","text":"Loss of maintained seizure protection","explanation":"Control while treated does not establish that interruption is safe."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"An interruption of chronic anticonvulsant treatment needs an authorized plan.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-carbamazepine--comprehensive--anticonvulsant_stop","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-carbamazepine::anticonvulsant_stop"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"The prescribed TEGRETOL — carbamazepine and the supplied product differ in release type or route. What establishes whether substitution is acceptable?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"A similar dosing interval listed on another patient’s chart","explanation":"Another regimen cannot establish product interchangeability."},{"id":"B","text":"An identical generic name and nominal milligram strength","explanation":"These do not establish the same release, route, or bioavailability."},{"id":"C","text":"Product-specific interchangeability and an authorized order","explanation":"Formulation differences require a defensible, authorized substitution."},{"id":"D","text":"A previously tolerated dose of the original formulation","e