rify product-specific interchangeability and authorization when route or release type differs.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin--comprehensive--formulation","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin::formulation"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"A concentration is near the upper laboratory reference limit during EPANUTIN — phenytoin therapy. Which information is necessary before interpreting it as clinically acceptable?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"The previous normal level without the recent dose history","explanation":"Earlier exposure does not establish current safety."},{"id":"B","text":"Dose/sample timing, organ function, and toxicity findings","explanation":"The result requires both sampling context and clinical interpretation."},{"id":"C","text":"The reference interval and prescribed dose without sample timing","explanation":"A mistimed result can be misleading despite a familiar dose."},{"id":"D","text":"The current symptom score without the level’s sampling context","explanation":"Clinical findings matter but cannot correct an unknown sampling time."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Interpret therapeutic drug concentrations with timing and clinical context.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin--comprehensive--drug_levels","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin::drug_levels"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"A patient taking phenytoin has low albumin, ataxia, and a total level reported within range. Which interpretation is most defensible?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Ataxia proves insufficient anticonvulsant exposure","explanation":"Ataxia is a toxicity signal, not proof of underdosing."},{"id":"B","text":"An in-range total value excludes toxicity despite the symptoms","explanation":"Total concentration alone can be misleading when binding changes."},{"id":"C","text":"Binding changes and clinical toxicity can make the total value misleading","explanation":"Interpret levels with albumin, organ function, and symptoms."},{"id":"D","text":"Low albumin lowers total levels and therefore excludes toxicity","explanation":"Less protein binding can increase the unbound fraction."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Protein binding and organ function affect interpretation of phenytoin levels.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin--comprehensive--phenytoin_albumin","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin::phenytoin_albumin"],"answerKey":"C"}],"questionCount":9,"model":"comprehensive-v1"}],"bankVersion":5,"legacyBankVersion":4,"sources":[{"id":"content-v35"},{"id":"label-ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin","title":"PHENYTOIN SODIUM CAPSULE, EXTENDED RELEASE [MAJOR PHARMACEUTICALS]","url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=46d5c0d1-a97b-46d9-8cf4-994780673337"}],"sourceFields":{"drugclass":"Hydantoin anticonvulsant; voltage-gated sodium-channel blocker.","mechanism":"Prolongs the inactivated state of voltage-gated sodium channels, limiting repetitive neuronal firing.","use":"Prevention/treatment of selected seizure disorders. In trauma/orthopaedic patients it may also appear when a patient has epilepsy or seizure risk from associated head injury; confirm the actual indication.","administration":"Use the exact ordered formulation and route. Oral Epanutin formulations are not automatically interchangeable dose-for-dose. If IV phenytoin is ordered, use the specific IV product/protocol and cardiac/BP monitoring requirements; do not infer IV instructions from an oral Epanutin pack.","monitor":"• Watch for nystagmus, ataxia, slurred speech, confusion and excessive sedation as possible toxicity. • Review serum phenytoin levels when ordered, especially with toxicity, poor seizure control, interacting drugs or formulation changes. • Check for rash/SJS-TEN and other hypersensitivity. • Review albumin, renal/hepatic status when interpreting levels. • Phenytoin has many drug interactions and should not be stopped abruptly without an authorized plan.","why":"Phenytoin reduces repetitive neuronal firing by stabilizing inactivated sodium channels, but its nonlinear pharmacokinetics and formulation differences make dose changes and interactions clinically important.","availability":"WARD-OBSERVED in IBD2 at Nasser Medical Complex in Oct 2026. Epanutin is a phenytoin brand. Formulations matter: some Epanutin products contain phenytoin sodium while others contain phenytoin, so verify the exact formulation and strength rather than assuming dose-form equivalence. ED shelf/drawer label photographed, 2 Nov 2026. This is a named compartment, not an independently audited stock count; check the package before use."},"readingSections":[{"field":"drugclass","label":"Drug class","text":"Hydantoin anticonvulsant; voltage-gated sodium-channel blocker.","id":"section-0-20a0a7a13bec37f0"},{"field":"mechanism","label":"Mechanism of action","text":"Prolongs the inactivated state of voltage-gated sodium channels, limiting repetitive neuronal firing.","id":"section-1-d08888ab1cefd720"},{"field":"use","label":"Main use","text":"Prevention/treatment of selected seizure disorders. In trauma/orthopaedic patients it may also appear when a patient has epilepsy or seizure risk from associated head injury; confirm the actual indication.","id":"section-2-12822c472f8ee2d4"},{"field":"administration","label":"Form & administration","text":"Use the exact ordered formulation and route. Oral Epanutin formulations are not automatically interchangeable dose-for-dose. If IV phenytoin is ordered, use the specific IV product/protocol and cardiac/BP monitoring requirements; do not infer IV instructions from an oral Epanutin pack.","id":"section-3-3e7ab98ec0e360c8"},{"field":"monitor","label":"Nursing considerations","text":"• Watch for nystagmus, ataxia, slurred speech, confusion and excessive sedation as possible toxicity. • Review serum phenytoin levels when ordered, especially with toxicity, poor seizure control, interacting drugs or formulation changes. • Check for rash/SJS-TEN and other hypersensitivity. • Review albumin, renal/hepatic status when interpreting levels. • Phenytoin has many drug interactions and should not be stopped abruptly without an authorized plan.","id":"section-4-00ee47718109fef6"},{"field":"why","label":"Essential rationale","text":"Phenytoin reduces repetitive neuronal firing by stabilizing inactivated sodium channels, but its nonlinear pharmacokinetics and formulation differences make dose changes and interactions clinically important.","id":"section-5-8c727f76dcd28194"},{"field":"availability","label":"Palestine availability","text":"WARD-OBSERVED in IBD2 at Nasser Medical Complex in Oct 2026. Epanutin is a phenytoin brand. Formulations matter: some Epanutin products contain phenytoin sodium while others contain phenytoin, so verify the exact formulation and strength rather than assuming dose-form equivalence. ED shelf/drawer label photographed, 2 Nov 2026. This is a named compartment, not an independently audited stock count; check the package before use.","id":"section-6-10d8061e1a4bd0dc"}],"legacyExams":[{"id":"ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin--standard","itemId":"ibd2-epanutin-phenytoin","itemType":"medication","title":"EPANUTIN — phenytoin","stage":"standard","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">=","percent":90,"roundBeforeComparison":false},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":"persisted total deadline: 90 seconds multiplied by question count"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"show keys and all option explanations after submission","retestPolicy":"same standard form after required reading","questions":[{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"What is the principal mechanism of action of EPANUTIN — phenytoin?","choices":[{"id":"A","text"