new factor synthesis while existing factors decline over time","explanation":"The full anticoagulant effect is delayed."},{"id":"D","text":"Warfarin irreversibly blocks platelet COX-1 before changing INR","explanation":"That describes aspirin’s primary platelet action."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Warfarin’s full effect is delayed relative to administration.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--7-day--warfarin_delay","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-warfarin-coumadin::warfarin_delay"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--advanced--warfarin_delay","answerKey":"C"},{"stem":"A warfarin-treated patient starts an interacting medicine or becomes acutely ill. Which follow-up most directly checks a changed anticoagulant response?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"INR trend and bleeding assessment","explanation":"Interaction or illness can alter warfarin response and bleeding risk."},{"id":"B","text":"QT interval and pulse-oximeter waveform","explanation":"These do not replace warfarin-specific monitoring."},{"id":"C","text":"SpO2 trend and inhaler technique","explanation":"These do not quantify the anticoagulant response."},{"id":"D","text":"Pain score and joint movement","explanation":"These do not establish changed anticoagulation intensity."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Medicines, illness, and diet changes can alter warfarin response.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--7-day--warfarin_interactions","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-warfarin-coumadin::warfarin_interactions"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--advanced--warfarin_interactions","answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"Two mechanical-valve patients have different prescribed INR targets. Which difference can justify this?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Presence versus absence of a pre-dose meal","explanation":"Meal timing is not the basis of the valve-specific target."},{"id":"B","text":"Valve type or position and patient thromboembolic risk","explanation":"These inform the patient-specific target."},{"id":"C","text":"Oral versus parenteral administration of warfarin maintenance","explanation":"The maintenance is oral and the target is not established this way."},{"id":"D","text":"Morning versus evening administration of the same warfarin dose","explanation":"Administration time does not define the valve-related target."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Mechanical-valve anticoagulation targets depend on valve and patient factors.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--7-day--mechanical_valve","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-warfarin-coumadin::mechanical_valve"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--advanced--mechanical_valve","answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Why does a mechanical valve create a continuing indication for prescribed anticoagulation?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Artificial non-endothelial surfaces and disturbed flow promote thrombus formation","explanation":"Anticoagulation reduces valve thrombosis and embolic risk."},{"id":"B","text":"The prosthesis requires routine dissolution of its structural material","explanation":"Anticoagulation does not dissolve the valve itself."},{"id":"C","text":"The prosthesis prevents circulating platelets from reaching the heart","explanation":"This is not the mechanism of valve-related thrombosis."},{"id":"D","text":"The prosthesis produces a permanent vitamin-K deficiency","explanation":"The thrombogenic surface, not vitamin-K deficiency, explains the indication."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Artificial valve surfaces and disturbed flow promote thrombosis and embolism.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--7-day--valve_thrombosis","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-warfarin-coumadin::valve_thrombosis"],"reusedFromQuestionId":"ccu-warfarin-coumadin--advanced--valve_thrombosis","answerKey":"A"}],"questionCount":14}],"scoringExclusions":[]},{"itemId":"ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime","title":"FORTUM — 