"A","text":"Carbapenem beta-lactam","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Third-generation cephalosporin beta-lactam antibacterial."},{"id":"B","text":"Third-generation cephalosporin","explanation":"Third-generation cephalosporin beta-lactam antibacterial."},{"id":"C","text":"Polyene antifungal","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Third-generation cephalosporin beta-lactam antibacterial."},{"id":"D","text":"Nitroimidazole","explanation":"The medicine is classified as: Third-generation cephalosporin beta-lactam antibacterial."}],"point":"Identify the drug class taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime--comprehensive--drug-class","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime::drug-class"],"answerKey":"B"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which is a clinical use of FORTUM — ceftazidime?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Treatment of susceptible serious Gram-negative infection","explanation":"This is a clinical use of the medicine: Treatment of susceptible bacterial infections, including serious gram-negative infection and Pseudomonas when appropriate. In orthopaedic/trauma care it may be used for susceptible wound, soft-tissue or other serious infections according to cultures and the antimicrobial plan."},{"id":"B","text":"Prevention of valve-related thromboembolism","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"C","text":"Suppression of ventricular ectopy by cardiac sodium-channel blockade","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"D","text":"Relief of bronchospasm by beta2 stimulation","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."}],"point":"Identify the main treatment role taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime--comprehensive--treatment-role","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime::treatment-role"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"Minutes after starting FORTUM — ceftazidime, a patient develops wheeze, facial swelling, and hypotension. Which reaction best fits?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Delayed marrow suppression","explanation":"This does not fit the rapid onset or the described manifestations."},{"id":"B","text":"Anaphylaxis","explanation":"Acute airway and circulatory compromise after exposure is strongly concerning."},{"id":"C","text":"Antibiotic-associated colitis","explanation":"This does not explain the immediate airway and circulatory pattern."},{"id":"D","text":"Isolated infusion-site phlebitis","explanation":"A local vein reaction does not explain the multisystem findings."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Review serious beta-lactam allergy and recognize anaphylaxis.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime--comprehensive--betalactam_allergy","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime::betalactam_allergy"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which result best informs assessment of accumulation risk and possible regimen adjustment for FORTUM — ceftazidime?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Creatinine trend and estimated GFR","explanation":"These inform renal clearance and regimen review."},{"id":"B","text":"INR trend and prothrombin time","explanation":"These assess a coagulation pathway rather than renal clearance."},{"id":"C","text":"ALT trend and serum bilirubin","explanation":"These assess hepatic injury rather than directly estimate renal clearance."},{"id":"D","text":"TSH trend and free thyroxine","explanation":"These assess thyroid function rather than renal elimination."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Renal impairment can require review of drug exposure and the prescribed regimen.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime--comprehensive--renal_dose","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime::renal_dose"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"During FORTUM — ceftazidime therapy, which new bowel pattern most warrants assessment for antibiotic-associated colitis?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Normal formed stool after breakfast","explanation":"This is not a new concerning diarrhea pattern."},{"id":"B","text":"Hard stool with straining","explanation":"This points toward constipation rather than colitis-related diarrhea."},{"id":"C","text":"Reduced stool frequency during immobility","explanation":"This does not identify the complication being tested."},{"id":"D","text":"Frequent, persistent watery diarrhea","explanation":"Persistent diarrhea during antibiotic exposure needs assessment for C. difficile and other causes."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Significant antibiotic-associated diarrhea requires evaluation.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime--comprehensive--antibiotic_diarrhea","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime::antibiotic_diarrhea"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"Which new neurological event during FORTUM — ceftazidime therapy needs the most urgent assessment?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"An unchanged chronic headache","explanation":"The case does not describe a new neurological deterioration in this option."},{"id":"B","text":"Mild unchanged nausea","explanation":"This is less urgent than a new seizure."},{"id":"C","text":"Improving original symptoms","explanation":"Therapeutic improvement does not itself identify neurotoxicity."},{"id":"D","text":"A new generalized seizure","explanation":"This is a potentially serious neurological adverse effect or another emergency."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Some treatments or their accumulation can provoke seizures.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime--comprehensive--seizure_risk","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ibd2-fortum-ceftazidime::seizure_risk"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"A bacterial infection is being treated with FORTUM — ceftazidime. Which paired findings most directly inform whether the antimicrobial plan remains suitable?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Fluid balance and serum sodium","explanation":"These inform hydration but do