es not treat the underlying cause of severe unexplained abdominal pain.","administration":"Give only by the ordered formulation/route. Injectable hyoscine butylbromide products are commonly given slow IV or IM depending on the product and order; rapid IV administration can cause marked hypotension. Verify the local ampoule label before preparation.","monitor":"• Watch for tachycardia, dry mouth, constipation, urinary retention and blurred vision/accommodation problems. • Contraindications/major cautions include narrow-angle glaucoma, myasthenia gravis, mechanical GI obstruction/ileus and urinary retention risk. • Persistent or worsening abdominal pain with fever, vomiting, hypotension, syncope or blood in stool requires evaluation rather than repeated symptomatic dosing. • Parenteral doses can rarely cause anaphylaxis.","why":"Blocks muscarinic acetylcholine receptors in peripheral smooth muscle, reducing gastrointestinal and genitourinary spasm.","availability":"WARD-REPORTED in the current rotation. Palestinian MoH lists SCOBUTYL ampoules containing hyoscine-N-butyl bromide 20 mg; verify ampoule volume, concentration and ordered route. Palestinian OTC records also list Scobutyl 10 mg tablets, so do not assume formulation from the brand name alone. ED shelf/drawer label photographed, 2 Nov 2026. This is a named compartment, not an independently audited stock count; check the package before use."},"readingSections":[{"field":"drugclass","label":"Drug class","text":"Antimuscarinic antispasmodic.","id":"section-0-d9273017864cdab8"},{"field":"mechanism","label":"Mechanism of action","text":"Peripheral antimuscarinic action reduces smooth-muscle spasm in the GI and genitourinary tracts.","id":"section-1-b2a2d33fdeda4760"},{"field":"use","label":"Main use","text":"Relieves smooth-muscle spasm, such as gastrointestinal, biliary or urinary tract colic/spasm. It treats spasm-related pain; it does not treat the underlying cause of severe unexplained abdominal pain.","id":"section-2-e4b43e0015b7d875"},{"field":"administration","label":"Form & administration","text":"Give only by the ordered formulation/route. Injectable hyoscine butylbromide products are commonly given slow IV or IM depending on the product and order; rapid IV administration can cause marked hypotension. Verify the local ampoule label before preparation.","id":"section-3-9544473b7af2941a"},{"field":"monitor","label":"Nursing considerations","text":"• Watch for tachycardia, dry mouth, constipation, urinary retention and blurred vision/accommodation problems. • Contraindications/major cautions include narrow-angle glaucoma, myasthenia gravis, mechanical GI obstruction/ileus and urinary retention risk. • Persistent or worsening abdominal pain with fever, vomiting, hypotension, syncope or blood in stool requires evaluation rather than repeated symptomatic dosing. • Parenteral doses can rarely cause anaphylaxis.","id":"section-4-eeb99a4b0ad7df71"},{"field":"why","label":"Essential rationale","text":"Blocks muscarinic acetylcholine receptors in peripheral smooth muscle, reducing gastrointestinal and genitourinary spasm.","id":"section-5-f518060a773c84bf"},{"field":"availability","label":"Palestine availability","text":"WARD-REPORTED in the current rotation. Palestinian MoH lists SCOBUTYL ampoules containing hyoscine-N-butyl bromide 20 mg; verify ampoule volume, concentration and ordered route. Palestinian OTC records also list Scobutyl 10 mg tablets, so do not assume formulation from the brand name alone. ED shelf/drawer label photographed, 2 Nov 2026. This is a named compartment, not an independently audited stock count; check the package before use.","id":"section-6-c5f30b40c62c98aa"}],"legacyExams":[{"id":"ibd2-scobutyl-hyoscine-butylbromide--standard","itemId":"ibd2-scobutyl-hyoscine-butylbromide","itemType":"medication","title":"SCOBUTYL — hyoscine-N-butyl bromide","stage":"standard","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">=","percent":90,"roundBeforeCo