d":"C"},{"text":"Tadalafil, finasteride and dutasteride","explanation":"Only tadalafil in this group inhibits PDE5.","id":"D"}],"point":"Recognize sildenafil, tadalafil and vardenafil as interacting PDE5 inhibitors.","criticalForSafety":true,"answerKey":"C","id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--comprehensive--nitrate_pde5","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::nitrate_pde5"],"revision":"drug-dependent-20261106","sourceFields":["monitor"]},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"A patient with sudden chest pain has scheduled oral isosorbide mononitrate and an authorized rapid-rescue plan. What property makes the maintenance tablet unsuitable as a substitute?","choices":[{"text":"The oral formulation has the same onset but a shorter duration than a sublingual rescue nitrate","explanation":"The important distinction is a slower onset, not a shorter duration.","id":"A"},{"text":"The oral formulation acts as an antiplatelet before acting as a vasodilator","explanation":"Its action is nitrate vasodilation and does not include an antiplatelet step.","id":"B"},{"text":"The oral formulation raises preload until the dose wears off","explanation":"Nitrate venodilation reduces preload. This does not account for rescue timing.","id":"C"},{"text":"The oral formulation cannot provide a sufficiently rapid onset for an acute episode","explanation":"A maintenance nitrate is not a substitute for the authorized acute chest-pain plan.","id":"D"}],"point":"Distinguish preventive duration from rapid onset.","criticalForSafety":true,"answerKey":"D","id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--comprehensive--nitrate_rescue","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::nitrate_rescue"],"revision":"drug-dependent-20261106","sourceFields":["use"]},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"The chart orders modified-release oral isosorbide mononitrate, but only immediate-release tablets of the same nominal strength are available. Which difference makes direct substitution inappropriate?","choices":[{"text":"The rate of release and the effective dosing schedule can differ","explanation":"The prescriber and pharmacist must verify a formulation-specific replacement regimen.","id":"A"},{"text":"The immediate-release tablet has an equivalent release profile at the same strength","explanation":"Equal labeled milligrams do not establish the same release profile.","id":"B"},{"text":"The modified-release formulation has a faster initial release and shorter scheduled interval by definition","explanation":"Modified release changes the release profile. This does not make it a faster equivalent.","id":"C"},{"text":"The approximate duration is determined by the milligrams alone","explanation":"Timing depends on formulation as well as dose.","id":"D"}],"point":"Identify release-dependent timing and exposure despite the same nominal strength.","criticalForSafety":true,"answerKey":"A","id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--comprehensive--formulation","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::formulation"],"revision":"drug-dependent-20261106","sourceFields":["administration"]}],"questionCount":7,"correctionRevision":"isosorbide-formulation-review-20261115","model":"comprehensive-v1"},{"id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--21-day","itemId":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate","itemType":"medication","title":"VASOCORE — isosorbide mononitrate","stage":"21-day","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"type":"error-count","allowedErrors":1},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":"untimed"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"incorrect, unanswered and unsure/guessed questions only after submission","retestPolicy":"same comprehensive exam and questions at every stage","questions":[{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which sequence explains the change in 