h is a clinical use of VASOCORE — isosorbide mononitrate?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Prevention and control of angina","explanation":"This is a clinical use of the medicine: Prevention/control of angina; not the rapid-rescue formulation for an acute angina attack."},{"id":"B","text":"Treatment of oral fungal lesions","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"C","text":"Replacement of glucose during severe hypoglycemia","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."},{"id":"D","text":"Suppression of gastric acid secretion","explanation":"This is a different treatment role."}],"point":"Identify the main treatment role taught for this medicine.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--standard--treatment-role","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::treatment-role"],"answerKey":"A"},{"stem":"A patient becomes light-headed on standing after VASOCORE — isosorbide mononitrate. Which paired assessment best checks the suspected adverse effect?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Resting temperature and infection symptoms","explanation":"These investigate infection rather than the suspected pressure effect."},{"id":"B","text":"Postural BP and associated symptoms","explanation":"A positional pressure fall can account for the light-headedness."},{"id":"C","text":"Visual acuity and accommodation symptoms","explanation":"These evaluate visual effects rather than establish a postural pressure fall."},{"id":"D","text":"Bowel frequency and abdominal distension","explanation":"These investigate a gastrointestinal effect rather than postural circulatory tolerance."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Recognize symptomatic hypotension during treatment.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--standard--hypotension","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::hypotension"],"answerKey":"B"},{"stem":"Which symptom pattern is compatible with nitrate vasodilation during VASOCORE — isosorbide mononitrate therapy?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Nystagmus with slurred speech","explanation":"This suggests a different neurological toxicity pattern."},{"id":"B","text":"Tendon pain with ankle swelling","explanation":"This points toward a different adverse-effect warning."},{"id":"C","text":"Headache with flushing or dizziness","explanation":"These are recognized nitrate effects; severity and BP still need assessment."},{"id":"D","text":"Mucosal rash with blistering","explanation":"This raises a different serious reaction concern."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Nitrate vasodilation commonly causes headache and dizziness.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--standard--nitrate_headache","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::nitrate_headache"],"answerKey":"C"}],"questionCount":5},{"id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--advanced","itemId":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate","itemType":"medication","title":"VASOCORE — isosorbide mononitrate","stage":"advanced","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"operator":">","percent":90,"roundBeforeComparison":false},"timing":{"timed":true,"secondsPerQuestion":90,"timerEnforcement":"persisted total deadline: 90 seconds multiplied by question count"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"show keys and all option explanations after submission","retestPolicy":"different from standard","questions":[{"stem":"A patient taking VASOCORE — isosorbide mononitrate has poor intake and a new BP fall when standing. Which factor best explains increased sensitivity to treatment?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Increased circulating volume","explanation":"This does not explain the volume-depleted presentation."},{"id":"B","text":"Increased vascular resistance","explanation":"This generally supports pressure rather than explaining the described fall."},{"id":"C","text":"Reduced gastrointestinal transit","explanation":"Slower transit does not account for the positional hemodynamic change."},{"id":"D","text":"Reduced circulating volume","explanation":"Volume depletion can amplify symptomatic hypotension."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"Recognize symptomatic hypotension during treatment.","criticalForSafety":false,"id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--advanced--hypotension","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::hypotension"],"answerKey":"D"},{"stem":"A patient due to receive VASOCORE — isosorbide mononitrate reports recent sildenafil use. What is the principal interaction concern?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"Excessive vasodilation and hypotension","explanation":"The combination can produce a dangerous pressure fall."},{"id":"B","text":"Excessive gastric acid secretion","explanation":"This is not the clinically important interaction."},{"id":"C","text":"Excessive clotting-factor synthesis","explanation":"These drugs do not combine through vitamin-K-dependent coagulation."},{"id":"D","text":"Excessive bacterial protein-synthesis inhibition","explanation":"Neither drug is acting as an antibacterial."}],"format":"single-best-answer","point":"PDE5 inhibitors and nitrates can cause profound hypotension.","criticalForSafety":true,"id":"ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate--advanced--nitrate_pde5","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-mononitrate::nitrate_pde5"],"answerKey":"A"},{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"A patient with sudden chest pain asks to use a maintenance isosorbide mononitrate tablet as rescue. Which distinction matters?","choices":[{"id":"A","text":"An identical nitrate class establishing an identical onset","explanation":"Shared class does not make maintenance and rescue products equivalent."},{"id":"B","text":"The tablet’s total milligrams establishing the speed of relief","explanation":"Dose size alone does not establish an appropriate rescue ons