g the SL tablet strength to set the rate","explanation":"The trade name and tablet strength cannot establish the IV preparation or rate.","id":"D"}],"point":"Require a separate product labeled for IV use with verified administration requirements.","criticalForSafety":true,"answerKey":"A","id":"ccu-isosorbide-dinitrate--comprehensive--formulation","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-dinitrate::formulation"],"revision":"drug-dependent-20261106","sourceFields":["administration"]}],"questionCount":8,"correctionRevision":"isosorbide-formulation-review-20261115","model":"comprehensive-v1"},{"id":"ccu-isosorbide-dinitrate--21-day","itemId":"ccu-isosorbide-dinitrate","itemType":"medication","title":"CORDIL — isosorbide dinitrate","stage":"21-day","reviewStatus":"authoring draft","passRule":{"type":"error-count","allowedErrors":1},"timing":{"timed":false,"secondsPerQuestion":null,"timerEnforcement":"untimed"},"scoring":{"correct":1,"incorrect":0,"unanswered":0,"partialCredit":false,"unsureOrGuessed":"review flag only","criticalSafetyMiss":"separate follow-up required; original numeric score unchanged"},"feedback":"incorrect, unanswered and unsure/guessed questions only after submission","retestPolicy":"same comprehensive exam and questions at every stage","questions":[{"format":"single-best-answer","stem":"Which signaling and vascular effect pair accounts for isosorbide dinitrate action?","choices":[{"text":"Increased nitric oxide signaling lowers cGMP and contracts vascular smooth muscle","explanation":"NO activates guanylate cyclase and raises cGMP.","id":"A"},{"text":"Increased nitric oxide signaling raises cGMP and relaxes vascular smooth muscle","explanation":"Organic nitrates increase NO signaling and cGMP, leading to relaxation.","id":"B"},{"text":"Increased beta1 signaling raises cAMP and directly relaxes veins","explanation":"Beta1 signaling is not the primary pathway for nitrate-induced vasodilation.","id":"C"},{"text":"Increased alpha1 signaling raises 