t dissolved in IV fluid with the same labeled mass","explanation":"The SL tablet is not a sterile IV dosage form and cannot fulfill the infusion order.","id":"B"},{"text":"An IV nitrate borrowed from another order with the same pump rate","explanation":"Different nitrate preparations and concentrations make copying a rate unsafe.","id":"C"},{"text":"An IV vial labeled only with the same trade name, using the SL tablet strength to set the rate","explanation":"The trade name and tablet strength cannot establish the IV preparation or rate.","id":"D"}],"point":"Require a separate product labeled for IV use with verified administration requirements.","criticalForSafety":true,"answerKey":"A","id":"ccu-isosorbide-dinitrate--comprehensive--formulation","points":1,"learningPointIds":["ccu-isosorbide-dinitrate::formulation"],"revision":"drug-dependent-20261106","sourceFields":["administration"]}],"questionCount":8,"correctionRevision":"isosorbide-formulation-review-20261115","model":"comprehensive-v1"}],"bankVersion":6,"legacyBankVersion":4,"sources":[{"id":"content-v35"},{"id":"label-ccu-isosorbide-dinitrate","title":"ISOSORBIDE DINITRATE TABLET [PAR HEALTH USA, LLC]","url":"https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/drugInfo.cfm?setid=6df6a2fa-c56c-4eb6-a485-c16585420eb0"}],"sourceFields":{"drugclass":"Organic nitrate vasodilator/antianginal.","mechanism":"Nitric-oxide/cGMP-mediated vasodilation.","use":"Faster nitrate relief than long-acting oral isosorbide mononitrate; IV nitrate therapy may be used for severe/unstable angina or refractory LV failure when specifically ordered.","administration":"For the documented SL product, place under the tongue and let dissolve. Do not treat an SL tablet as an IV product. IV ISDN exists internationally as a controlled infusion, so any IV vial must be verified from the exact product before use.","monitor":"• Check BP before and after use. • Headache, flushing and dizziness are common. • Check for PDE-5 inhibitor exposure. • If an IV nitrate is ordered, verify the exact product, concentration, tubing and infusion method.","why":"Route determines onset and delivery; nitrate vasodilation can rapidly lower BP.","availability":"YES for the Palestinian 5-mg sublingual form. A Palestinian IV isosorbide-dinitrate product was not publicly confirmed in the trolley research; Palestine separately lists IV nitroglycerin. ED shelf/drawer label photographed, 2 Nov 2026. This is a named compartment, not an independently audited stock count; check the package before use. User confirmed on 2 Nov 2026 that Cordil is isosorbide in their ED. Existing reference identifies CORDIL 5 mg as sublingual isosorbide dinitrate; user did not specify the mono-/dinitrate salt or release form, so check the physical product before using formulation-specific advice."},"readingSections":[{"field":"drugclass","label":"Drug class","text":"Organic nitrate vasodilator/antianginal.","id":"section-0-310e3f0d938a9df9"},{"field":"mechanism","label":"Mechanism of action","text":"Nitric-oxide/cGMP-mediated vasodilation.","id":"section-1-0341c50e7e6fd0b2"},{"field":"use","label":"Main use","text":"Faster nitrate relief than long-acting oral isosorbide mononitrate; IV nitrate therapy may be used for severe/unstable angina or refractory LV failure when specifically ordered.","id":"section-2-0fcbf0ace5b6ed03"},{"field":"administration","label":"Form & administration","text":"For the documented SL product, place under the tongue and let dissolve. Do not treat an SL tablet as an IV product. IV ISDN exists internationally as a controlled infusion, so any IV vial must be verified from the exact product before use.","id":"section-3-47fb98ee9db5799e"},{"field":"monitor","label":"Nursing considerations","text":"• Check BP before and after use. • Headache, flushing and dizziness are common. • Check for PDE-5 inhibitor exposure. • If an IV nitrate is ordered, verify the exact product, concentration, tubing and infusion method.","id":"section-4-fb0cffa5cb4dcb2a"